BT /F1 10 Tf 54 720 Td (A full charge takes approximately 4 hours at 20 C. A fully charged HX-BAT-200 gives a typical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 707 Td (runtime of 36 hours at 20 C, the longest of the Halcyon family because only one sensor is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 694 Td (powered. Charge only between 0 and +40 C.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 672 Td (The HX-200 does not fit the HX-DOCK-4 directly. To use the docking station, fit the HX-200 into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 659 Td (the HX-ADP-200 adapter first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 637 Td (On power-on the instrument tests the LEDs, sounder and vibration motor, displays the firmware) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 624 Td (version \(3.2.4\), the alarm set points and the days until calibration and bump test are due,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 611 Td (then warms up for 30 seconds before entering measuring mode.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 586 Td (6. Alarms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 564 Td (Factory default set points for the HX-200:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 543 Td (Alarm | Set point) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 531 Td (Low | 5 ppm H2S) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 519 Td (High | 10 ppm H2S) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 507 Td (STEL \(15 min\) | 15 ppm H2S) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 495 Td (TWA \(8 h\) | 5 ppm H2S) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 473 Td (The low alarm is non-latching by default. The high alarm latches until acknowledged with ON/OK) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 460 Td (in clean air. STEL and TWA alarms cannot be acknowledged until the instrument is switched off.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 447 Td (Set points can be changed only in the supervisor menu \(Menu > Supervisor > Alarms > Set Points\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 434 Td (or with Meridian Link.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 409 Td (7. Bump testing and calibration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 387 Td (Bump test the HX-200 before each day's use. Fit the calibration cap and apply MI-CAL-H2S25 \(25) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 374 Td (ppm H2S in nitrogen\) at 0.5 L/min using the MI-REG-05 regulator. The bump test passes if the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 361 Td (reading reaches at least 20 ppm within 45 seconds and the alarms operate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 339 Td (The HX-200 must be calibrated at least every 180 days. Unlike the HX-210, the HX-200 interval) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326 Td (was not changed in 2025; it remains 180 days. Calibration uses MI-CAL-H2S25 at 0.5 L/min with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 313 Td (span stabilisation wait of 90 seconds. Select Menu > Calibrate, perform the fresh-air zero,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 300 Td (then apply gas when prompted. If the span fails, the instrument shows E-104.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 275 Td (8. Datalogging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 253 Td (The HX-200 logs H2S readings at a 1-minute interval. At that interval the datalog holds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 240 Td (approximately 60 days. The event log holds the last 250 events. Logs are downloaded with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 227 Td (Meridian Link or the HX-DOCK-4 \(with HX-ADP-200\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 202 Td (9. Maintenance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 180 Td (Clean with a damp cloth and mild detergent only. Replace the dust membrane HX-MEM-200 every 6) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 167 Td (months. Check remaining sensor life at Menu > Instrument > Service > Sensor Life.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 145 Td (The rear housing of the HX-200 is held by four Torx T8 screws. Tighten them to 0.35 N m when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 132 Td (refitting. The rear gasket is HX-GSK-200.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 107 Td (10. Supervisor settings) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 85 Td (The factory default supervisor passcode for the HX-200 is 2007. Change it on commissioning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 72 Td (using Menu > Supervisor > Security > Change Passcode. After five incorrect entries the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 59 Td (supervisor menu is locked for 10 minutes. The calibration interval can be set between 30 and) Tj ET
endstream
