BT /F2 13 Tf 54 368 Td (13. Storage and disposal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346 Td (Store the HX-200 switched off in a clean, dry area between 0 and +30 C. For storage longer than) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 333 Td (30 days, charge the HX-BAT-200 to between 40% and 60% and recharge it every 3 months. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 320 Td (calibration countdown continues during storage; an instrument stored for more than 180 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 307 Td (must be calibrated before use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 285 Td (At the end of its life, return the HX-200 to Meridian or to an approved WEEE collection point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272 Td (Remove the battery pack and dispose of it separately. The H2S sensor contains acid electrolyte) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 259 Td (and must be treated as hazardous waste.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 234 Td (14. Document history) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 213 Td (Revision | Date | Changes) Tj ET
